The simulation in m2/sim and m2/game, and the sprites, sounds, font glyphs and strings
exported into m3/assets, m4/assets and m2/dos-rt/src/ui_data.rs, come from
liminal-hq/lieutenant-fizz (Apache-2.0 OR MIT).

The sound converters in m4/sound keep the headers they were written with (MIT, or Apache-2.0 OR MIT for the voice
data generated from the main game); they import @liminal-hq/undertone (MIT), which the exporter installs with Bun.

Third-party material shipped beside the game or linked into it:

CWSDPMI (dist/fizz-dos-demo/CWSDPMI.EXE, with its notes in CWSDPMI.DOC)
  A DOS protected-mode extender, Copyright (C) 1995-2010 Charles W Sandmann. Its binary
  distribution may be redistributed unmodified, with CWSDPMI.DOC, under the terms in that file.
  FIZZ.EXE needs it beside it to start.

FreeDOS 1.4 (KERNEL.SYS, COMMAND.COM and the boot code on the -floppy-freedos.img image of a release)
  GPL-2.0. https://www.freedos.org; the image carries FREEDOS.TXT, with the licence and where the source is.
  tools/make-freedos-floppy.sh downloads the 1.4 Floppy Edition, checks it against a pinned SHA-256 and
  copies those files in. The game disk and zips do not carry them.

DJGPP (linked into FIZZ.EXE)
  The cross-compiler and its C library and runtime come from https://www.delorie.com/djgpp/ and
  are downloaded by tools/fetch-tools.sh into vendor/, which is not committed. Their licence
  terms are in the DJGPP distribution.

DOSBox Staging (used to run the game headless in tools/dosrun.sh; not distributed here)
  GPL-2.0-or-later. https://www.dosbox-staging.org

js-dos (site/vendor/js-dos, which runs the game in a browser)
  GPL-2.0, with its licence and provenance beside it. It is served as a separate program next
  to the page and the game bundle; it does not change the licence of the game's own code.
